-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE YOU START
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You need:

  * DaVinci Resolve, already installed and working
  * Python 3 on your computer
      macOS:   https://www.python.org/downloads/  (or: brew install python3)
      Windows: https://www.python.org/downloads/
               IMPORTANT: tick "Add Python to PATH" during setup
  * An internet connection, for the first installation only
  * About 5-10 minutes

Close DaVinci Resolve before installing. Reopen it when you are done.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
macOS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File to use:  MarkerClipManager___VERSION___Install_macOS.command

  1. RIGHT-CLICK the file, then choose "Open".
     Do NOT double-click it.

     Why: the installer is not signed with an Apple developer certificate,
     so a normal double-click is blocked with a message about an
     "unidentified developer". Right-click > Open gives you a dialog with
     an "Open" button, which a double-click does not.

  2. In the dialog that appears, click "Open".
     A Terminal window opens and shows the progress.

  3. Wait. The installer does two things:
       [1/2] copies the script files
       [2/2] prepares the Python environment (downloads PySide6)

     Step 2 downloads roughly 150 MB and can take a few minutes.
     It is normal for the window to look still while this happens.

  4. When you read "Installazione completata", press ENTER to close.

Where it installs:

  Script files:
    ~/Library/Application Support/Blackmagic Design/DaVinci Resolve/
      Fusion/Scripts/Comp/MarkerClipManager/

  Python environment (separate, does not touch your system Python):
    ~/.venvs/resolve_pyside6/


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WINDOWS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File to use:  MarkerClipManager___VERSION___Install_Windows.cmd

  1. DOUBLE-CLICK the file.

     If Windows SmartScreen shows a blue warning window
     ("Windows protected your PC"), click "More info", then "Run anyway".
     This happens because the installer is not signed.

  2. A command window opens and shows the progress:
       [1/2] copies the script files
       [2/2] installs PySide6 (downloads roughly 150 MB)

  3. When you read "Installazione completata", press a key to close.

Where it installs:

  Script files, in whichever of these two folders already exists on your PC:
    %APPDATA%\Blackmagic Design\DaVinci Resolve\Support\Fusion\Scripts\Comp\MarkerClipManager\
    %APPDATA%\Blackmagic Design\DaVinci Resolve\Fusion\Scripts\Comp\MarkerClipManager\

  PySide6 is installed for your user account only, in the Python that
  Windows finds first. It does not require administrator rights.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFTER INSTALLATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open DaVinci Resolve, open a project with a timeline, then:

    Workspace  >  Scripts  >  Comp  >  MarkerClipManager

The interface opens in its own window. It starts in your system language if
one of the 12 translations matches, otherwise in English. You can change the
language from the menu in the header (it takes effect after a restart).


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"The installer said Python was not found"
    The script files ARE installed, only the Python part is missing.
    Install Python 3 (see BEFORE YOU START), then run the installer again.

"The installer said PySide6 could not be installed"
    Usually no internet connection. The script files ARE installed.
    Once you are online, open the installed folder and run:
      macOS:    MarkerClipManager_Setup.command
      Windows:  MarkerClipManager_Setup_Windows.cmd
    These only redo the Python part, they do not reinstall everything.

"MarkerClipManager does not appear in the Scripts menu"
    Resolve reads that folder when it starts: quit Resolve completely and
    reopen it. On Windows, if it still does not appear, the files may have
    gone to the other of the two folders listed above — move the
    MarkerClipManager folder to the one Resolve actually uses.

"It appears in the menu but nothing opens, or an error mentions PySide6"
    On Windows this usually means you have more than one Python installed,
    and PySide6 ended up in a different one from the one Resolve uses.
    Run MarkerClipManager_Setup_Windows.cmd from the installed folder; if it
    still fails, install PySide6 into the Python that Resolve uses.

    Note: on Windows the script cannot fall back to a dedicated Python
    environment the way it does on macOS. PySide6 must be available in the
    Python that Resolve itself runs.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATING AND UNINSTALLING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To update: run the new installer. It overwrites the script files and leaves
your settings alone (see below). No need to remove the old version first.

Not touched by an installation or an update:
    ~/Library/Application Support/RepertoireDB/     (macOS)
    %USERPROFILE%\Library\Application Support\RepertoireDB\   (Windows)
  This is where your language preference lives.

To uninstall: delete the MarkerClipManager folder from the Scripts location,
and — on macOS, if you use it for nothing else — the folder
~/.venvs/resolve_pyside6/


